{"id":"mahabharata-12-309","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":309,"title":"नवाधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 309 · Shuka's turning away from the world","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how Shuka, the son of Vyasa, came to disgust with the world, and Bhishma tells how Vyasa taught him of the hells and the suffering of the unwise. He tells how Vyasa urged his son to gather dharma in his youth, and Shuka left his father for the path of liberation.","kn":"ವ್ಯಾಸಪುತ್ರ ಶುಕನಿಗೆ ಲೋಕದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ವೈರಾಗ್ಯ ಹೇಗೆ ಬಂತೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ನರಕ, ಅಜ್ಞಾನಿಗಳ ದುಃಖವನ್ನು ವ್ಯಾಸ ಬೋಧಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯೌವನದಲ್ಲೇ ಧರ್ಮ ಸಂಚಯ ಮಾಡಲು ವ್ಯಾಸ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸಿದ, ಶುಕ ತಂದೆಯನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಮೋಕ್ಷ ಮಾರ್ಗ ಹಿಡಿದ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि व्यासपुत्र शुक को संसार से वैराग्य कैसे हुआ, और भीष्म बताते हैं कि व्यास ने उन्हें नरकों और अज्ञानियों के दुःख की शिक्षा दी। वे बताते हैं कि व्यास ने पुत्र से यौवन में धर्म-संचय करने को कहा और शुक पिता को छोड़कर मोक्ष के मार्ग पर चले गए।","te":"వ్యాస పుత్రుడు శుకునికి లోకంపై వైరాగ్యం ఎలా కలిగిందని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; వ్యాసుడు నరకాలు, అజ్ఞానుల దుఃఖం బోధించిన తీరును భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. యవ్వనంలోనే ధర్మ సంచయం చేయమని వ్యాసుడు కొడుకును ప్రేరేపించగా శుకుడు తండ్రిని విడిచి మోక్ష మార్గం పట్టాడు.","ta":"வியாசரின் மகன் சுகருக்கு உலகில் வெறுப்பு எவ்வாறு வந்தது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, நரகங்களையும் அறிவிலிகளின் துன்பத்தையும் வியாசர் போதித்ததைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். இளமையிலேயே தர்மத்தைச் சேர்க்குமாறு வியாசர் மகனை வற்புறுத்த, சுகர் தந்தையை விட்டு விடுதலை வழியில் சென்றார்.","ml":"വ്യാസപുത്രനായ ശുകൻ ലോകത്തോട് വിരക്തി നേടിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; നരകങ്ങളെയും അജ്ഞരുടെ ദുരിതങ്ങളെയും കുറിച്ച് വ്യാസൻ പഠിപ്പിച്ചതെന്തെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. യൗവനത്തിൽ തന്നെ ധർമ്മം ശേഖരിക്കാൻ വ്യാസൻ മകനെ പ്രേരിപ്പിച്ചതും, മോക്ഷത്തിന്റെ വഴിക്കായി ശുകൻ പിതാവിനെ വിട്ടുപോയതും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.309; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथं निर्वेदमापन्नः शुको वैयासकिः पुरा ।\nएतदिच्छामि कौरव्य श्रोतुं कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did Shuka, son of Vyasa, come to be filled with disgust for the world long ago? I wish to hear this, Kaurava, for I am curious."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"प्राकृतेन सुवृत्तेन चरन्तमकुतोभयम् ।\nअध्याप्य कृत्स्नं स्वाध्यायमन्वशाद्वै पिता सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having taught his son, who lived fearless in simple good conduct, the whole of the Veda, his father Vyasa instructed him:"}},{"n":3,"text":"धर्मं पुत्र निषेवस्व सुतीक्ष्णौ हि हिमातपौ ।\nक्षुत्पिपासे च वायुं च जय नित्यं जितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Practice dharma, my son; cold and heat are very sharp. Always conquer hunger, thirst and wind, with your senses mastered.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"सत्यमार्जवमक्रोधमनसूयां दमं तपः ।\nअहिंसां चानृशंस्यं च विधिवत्परिपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Rightly maintain truth, uprightness, freedom from anger and envy, self-control, austerity, non-violence and kindness.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"सत्ये तिष्ठ रतो धर्मे हित्वा सर्वमनार्जवम् ।\nदेवतातिथिशेषेण यात्रां प्राणस्य संश्रय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Stand in truth, delighting in dharma, abandoning all crookedness; and support your life with what remains after serving gods and guests.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"फेनपात्रोपमे देहे जीवे शकुनिवत्स्थिते ।\nअनित्ये प्रियसंवासे कथं स्वपिषि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In a body like a vessel of foam, with the life in it perched like a bird, impermanent though dear to dwell in, how can you sleep, my boy?\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अप्रमत्तेषु जाग्रत्सु नित्ययुक्तेषु शत्रुषु ।\nअन्तरं लिप्समानेषु बालस्त्वं नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Enemies are watchful, alert and always at work, seeking an opening; you are a child and do not see it.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"गण्यमानेषु वर्षेषु क्षीयमाणे तथायुषि ।\nजीविते शिष्यमाणे च किमुत्थाय न धावसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"While the years are being counted, life is wearing away and life is running down, why do you not rise and run?\""}},{"n":9,"text":"ऐहलौकिकमीहन्ते मांसशोणितवर्धनम् ।\nपारलौकिककार्येषु प्रसुप्ता भृशनास्तिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They strive for this world, fattening flesh and blood, but are fast asleep in matters of the next world, the thorough unbelievers.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"धर्माय येऽभ्यसूयन्ति बुद्धिमोहान्विता नराः ।\nअपथा गच्छतां तेषामनुयातापि पीड्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Men who, deluded in mind, scorn dharma suffer even as followers of those who go on wrong paths.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"ये तु तुष्टाः सुनियताः सत्यागमपरायणाः ।\nधर्म्यं पन्थानमारूढास्तानुपास्स्व च पृच्छ च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But those who are content, well restrained, devoted to true scripture, and set on the path of dharma: serve them and question them.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"उपधार्य मतं तेषां वृद्धानां धर्मदर्शिनाम् ।\nनियच्छ परया बुद्ध्या चित्तमुत्पथगामि वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having taken in the view of those old men who see dharma, restrain with supreme understanding the mind that wanders off the path.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अद्यकालिकया बुद्ध्या दूरे श्व इति निर्भयाः ।\nसर्वभक्षा न पश्यन्ति कर्मभूमिं विचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With a mind that lives for today, thinking 'tomorrow is far off', the fearless, eating anything, the senseless do not see the field of action.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"धर्मनिःश्रेणिमास्थाय किंचित्किंचित्समारुह ।\nकोशकारवदात्मानं वेष्टयन्नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Take the ladder of dharma and climb a little at a time; you do not see that you are wrapping yourself like a silkworm.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"नास्तिकं भिन्नमर्यादं कूलपातमिवास्थिरम् ।\nवामतः कुरु विस्रब्धो नरं वेणुमिवोद्धतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Turn confidently away the unbeliever who breaks bounds, unstable like a crumbling riverbank, like a raised bamboo, and set him to the left.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"कामं क्रोधं च मृत्युं च पञ्चेन्द्रियजलां नदीम् ।\nनावं धृतिमयीं कृत्वा जन्मदुर्गाणि संतर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Make steadiness a boat and cross the river of desire, anger and death, whose waters are the five senses, and pass the hard places of birth.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"मृत्युनाभ्याहते लोके जरया परिपीडिते ।\nअमोघासु पतन्तीषु धर्मयानेन संतर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When the world is struck by death and tormented by old age, and unfailing days are falling, cross by the vehicle of dharma.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"तिष्ठन्तं च शयानं च मृत्युरन्वेषते यदा ।\nनिर्वृतिं लभसे कस्मादकस्मान्मृत्युनाशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When death hunts you whether standing or lying, how can you find rest? You will be destroyed by death out of the blue.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"संचिन्वानकमेवैनं कामानामवितृप्तकम् ।\nवृकीवोरणमासाद्य मृत्युरादाय गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As a she-wolf takes a lamb, death takes one who is still gathering and unsatisfied with desires.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"क्रमशः संचितशिखो धर्मबुद्धिमयो महान् ।\nअन्धकारे प्रवेष्टव्ये दीपो यत्नेन धार्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Little by little the great flame is built up, made of the understanding of dharma; when you must enter darkness, hold a lamp carefully.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"संपतन्देहजालानि कदाचिदिह मानुषे ।\nब्राह्मण्यं लभते जन्तुस्तत्पुत्र परिपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Falling through the nets of bodies, a creature once in a while gains brahminhood in the human world; guard that, my son.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"ब्राह्मणस्य हि देहोऽयं न कामार्थाय जायते ।\nइह क्लेशाय तपसे प्रेत्य त्वनुपमं सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This body of a brahmin is not born for desire and wealth; it is for toil and austerity here and incomparable happiness hereafter.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"ब्राह्मण्यं बहुभिरवाप्यते तपोभि-\nस्तल्लब्ध्वा न परिपणेन हेडितव्यम् ।\nस्वाध्याये तपसि दमे च नित्ययुक्तः\nक्षेमार्थी कुशलपरः सदा यतस्व ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahminhood is gained through many austerities; having gained it, do not squander it for a petty price. Ever intent on study, austerity and self-control, strive always, seeking well-being and skilled."}},{"n":24,"text":"अव्यक्तप्रकृतिरयं कलाशरीरः\nसूक्ष्मात्मा क्षणत्रुटिशो निमेषरोमा ।\nऋत्वास्यः समबलशुक्लकृष्णनेत्रो\nमासाङ्गो द्रवति वयोहयो नराणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This running horse of the ages of men has an unmanifest nature, a body of parts, a subtle self, with moments and instants for hairs, seasons for a face, and eyes of equal strength, white and black, and months as limbs."}},{"n":25,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा प्रसृतमजस्रमुग्रवेगं\nगच्छन्तं सततमिहाव्यपेक्षमाणम् ।\nचक्षुस्ते यदि न परप्रणेतृनेयं\nधर्मे ते भवतु मनः परं निशम्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it spread and ceaselessly swift, always going without looking back, if your eye is not led by others, then, hearing this, let your mind turn to dharma."}},{"n":26,"text":"येऽमी तु प्रचलितधर्मकामवृत्ताः\nक्रोशन्तः सततमनिष्टसंप्रयोगाः ।\nक्लिश्यन्ते परिगतवेदनाशरीरा\nबह्वीभिः सुभृशमधर्मवासनाभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have strayed from dharma and desire, always crying out, joined with the unwanted, suffer in bodies full of pain, with many deep impressions of wrongdoing."}},{"n":27,"text":"राजा धर्मपरः सदा शुभगोप्ता\nसमीक्ष्य सुकृतिनां दधाति लोकान् ।\nबहुविधमपि चरतः प्रदिशति\nसुखमनुपगतं निरवद्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king devoted to dharma, ever a good protector, assigns worlds to the righteous after examining; even for those who act in many ways he grants blameless happiness not previously reached."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्वानो भीषणायोमुखानि वयांसि\nवडगृध्रकुलपक्षिणां च संघाः ।\nनरां कदने रुधिरपा गुरुवचन-\nनुदमुपरतं विशसन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dogs, fearful iron-mouthed birds and flocks of vultures and other birds, drinking blood in battle, tear apart the one who has ceased to obey his elders."}},{"n":29,"text":"मर्यादा नियताः स्वयंभुवा य इहेमाः\nप्रभिनत्ति दशगुणा मनोनुगत्वात् ।\nनिवसति भृशमसुखं पितृविषय-\nविपिनमवगाह्य स पापः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, following the mind, breaks the ten limits set by the Self-born here lives in great misery, having entered the forest of the ancestors' domain; he is sinful."}},{"n":30,"text":"यो लुब्धः सुभृशं प्रियानृतश्च मनुष्यः\nसततनिकृतिवञ्चनारतिः स्यात् ।\nउपनिधिभिरसुखकृत्स परमनिरयगो\nभृशमसुखमनुभवति दुष्कृतकर्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who is greedy, very fond of lies, always delighting in cheating and fraud, who causes suffering through deposits, goes to the worst hell and, an evildoer, suffers great misery."}},{"n":31,"text":"उष्णां वैतरणीं महानदी-\nमवगाढोऽसिपत्रवनभिन्नगात्रः ।\nपरशुवनशयो निपतितो\nवसति च महानिरये भृशार्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plunged in the hot river Vaitarani and with limbs cut by the sword-leaf forest, lying in the forest of axes, he falls and dwells in the great hell, in terrible torment."}},{"n":32,"text":"महापदानि कत्थसे न चाप्यवेक्षसे परम् ।\nचिरस्य मृत्युकारिकामनागतां न बुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You boast of great things yet do not look beyond; you do not perceive the long-approaching, death-making future."}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रयास्यतां किमास्यते समुत्थितं महद्भयम् ।\nअतिप्रमाथि दारुणं सुखस्य संविधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great fear has risen for those departing; why do you sit? Arrange for happiness against what is crushing and cruel."}},{"n":34,"text":"पुरा मृतः प्रणीयसे यमस्य मृत्युशासनात् ।\nतदन्तिकाय दारुणैः प्रयत्नमार्जवे कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before you are taken dead by the order of Yama's death, strive honestly against those cruel ones."}},{"n":35,"text":"पुरा समूलबान्धवं प्रभुर्हरत्यदुःखवित् ।\nतवेह जीवितं यमो न चास्ति तस्य वारकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before the lord, who knows no pain, carries off relatives with their roots, Yama is your life here and there is no one to hold him back."}},{"n":36,"text":"पुरा विवाति मारुतो यमस्य यः पुरःसरः ।\nपुरैक एव नीयसे कुरुष्व सांपरायिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before the wind blows that goes before Yama, you will be led alone; do what concerns the beyond."}},{"n":37,"text":"पुरा सहिक्क एव ते प्रवाति मारुतोऽन्तकः ।\nपुरा च विभ्रमन्ति ते दिशो महाभयागमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before that wind, the Ender, blows to you with a hiccup, and before the directions whirl at the coming of great fear..."}},{"n":38,"text":"स्मृतिश्च संनिरुध्यते पुरा तवेह पुत्रक ।\nसमाकुलस्य गच्छतः समाधिमुत्तमं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"...and before your memory is blocked here, my son, when you go confused, make the highest concentration."}},{"n":39,"text":"कृताकृते शुभाशुभे प्रमादकर्मविप्लुते ।\nस्मरन्पुरा न तप्यसे निधत्स्व केवलं निधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Done and undone, good and bad, ruined by heedless deeds: remembering these before, you will not burn; lay up only that treasure."}},{"n":40,"text":"पुरा जरा कलेवरं विजर्जरीकरोति ते ।\nबलाङ्गरूपहारिणी निधत्स्व केवलं निधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before old age wears out your body, stealing strength, limbs and beauty, lay up only that treasure."}},{"n":41,"text":"पुरा शरीरमन्तको भिनत्ति रोगसायकैः ।\nप्रसह्य जीवितक्षये तपो महत्समाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before the Ender breaks the body with arrows of disease, practice great austerity, forcing it, as life runs out."}},{"n":42,"text":"पुरा वृका भयंकरा मनुष्यदेहगोचराः ।\nअभिद्रवन्ति सर्वतो यतस्व पुण्यशीलने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before the fearsome wolves who range over human bodies run at you from all sides, strive in the practice of merit."}},{"n":43,"text":"पुरान्धकारमेककोऽनुपश्यसि त्वरस्व वै ।\nपुरा हिरण्मयान्नगान्निरीक्षसेऽद्रिमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before you see alone the darkness and the golden mountains on the mountaintop, hurry."}},{"n":44,"text":"पुरा कुसंगतानि ते सुहृन्मुखाश्च शत्रवः ।\nविचालयन्ति दर्शनाद्घटस्व पुत्र यत्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before bad company, and enemies with friendly faces, distract you from seeing, my son, strive for the highest."}},{"n":45,"text":"धनस्य यस्य राजतो भयं न चास्ति चौरतः ।\nमृतं च यन्न मुञ्चति समर्जयस्व तद्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gather that wealth which a king cannot threaten, nor a thief, and which does not leave you at death."}},{"n":46,"text":"न तत्र संविभज्यते स्वकर्मभिः परस्परम् ।\nयदेव यस्य यौतकं तदेव तत्र सोऽश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"There it is not divided among people by their own actions; whatever belongs to someone as his own, that he enjoys there."}},{"n":47,"text":"परत्र येन जीव्यते तदेव पुत्र दीयताम् ।\nधनं यदक्षयं ध्रुवं समर्जयस्व तत्स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give, my son, that by which one lives in the next world; earn for yourself that wealth which is imperishable and steady."}},{"n":48,"text":"न यावदेव पच्यते महाजनस्य यावकम् ।\nअपक्व एव यावके पुरा प्रणीयसे त्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before the great people's barley is cooked, before it is cooked, you are carried off; hurry."}},{"n":49,"text":"न मातृपितृबान्धवा न संस्तुतः प्रियो जनः ।\nअनुव्रजन्ति संकटे व्रजन्तमेकपातिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither mother, father, kinsmen nor loved friends follow one who goes alone in distress, falling alone."}},{"n":50,"text":"यदेव कर्म केवलं स्वयं कृतं शुभाशुभम् ।\nतदेव तस्य यौतकं भवत्यमुत्र गच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever action he alone has himself done, good or bad, that is his provision as he goes to the next world."}},{"n":51,"text":"हिरण्यरत्नसंचयाः शुभाशुभेन संचिताः ।\nन तस्य देहसंक्षये भवन्ति कार्यसाधकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Piles of gold and jewels gathered by good or bad means do not accomplish his purpose when the body is destroyed."}},{"n":52,"text":"परत्रगामिकस्य ते कृताकृतस्य कर्मणः ।\nन साक्षिरात्मना समो नृणामिहास्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no witness equal to the Self for the done and undone actions of you who are going to the next world, among men here."}},{"n":53,"text":"मनुष्यदेहशून्यकं भवत्यमुत्र गच्छतः ।\nप्रपश्य बुद्धिचक्षुषा प्रदृश्यते हि सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The human body is empty for one going there; look with the eye of understanding, for it is seen all around."}},{"n":54,"text":"इहाग्निसूर्यवायवः शरीरमाश्रितास्त्रयः ।\nत एव तस्य साक्षिणो भवन्ति धर्मदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here fire, sun and wind, three, dwell in the body; they themselves become the witnesses of the one who sees dharma."}},{"n":55,"text":"यथानिशेषु सर्वतःस्पृशत्सु सर्वदारिषु ।\nप्रकाशगूढवृत्तिषु स्वधर्ममेव पालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Amid the nights that touch everyone and tear all, with their ways of light and of concealment, guard your own dharma alone."}},{"n":56,"text":"अनेकपारिपन्थिके विरूपरौद्ररक्षिते ।\nस्वमेव कर्म रक्ष्यतां स्वकर्म तत्र गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"On a road with many obstructions, guarded by shapes terrible and cruel, guard your own action; your own action goes there."}},{"n":57,"text":"न तत्र संविभज्यते स्वकर्मणा परस्परम् ।\nयथाकृतं स्वकर्मजं तदेव भुज्यते फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There it is not shared with others through one's own action; as done, so the fruit born of one's action is enjoyed."}},{"n":58,"text":"यथाप्सरोगणाः फलं सुखं महर्षिभिः सह ।\nतथाप्नुवन्ति कर्मतो विमानकामगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As troops of apsaras find fruit and happiness with great sages, so those who travel at will in celestial cars find it through action."}},{"n":59,"text":"यथेह यत्कृतं शुभं विपाप्मभिः कृतात्मभिः ।\nतदाप्नुवन्ति मानवास्तथा विशुद्धयोनयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What good has been done here by those free of sin and whose selves are made, that men of pure birth attain."}},{"n":60,"text":"प्रजापतेः सलोकतां बृहस्पतेः शतक्रतोः ।\nव्रजन्ति ते परां गतिं गृहस्थधर्मसेतुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the bridges of the householder's dharma, they go to the supreme goal, to a world shared with Prajapati, Brihaspati and Indra."}},{"n":61,"text":"सहस्रशोऽप्यनेकशः प्रवक्तुमुत्सहामहे ।\nअबुद्धिमोहनं पुनः प्रभुर्विना न यावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We can say it thousands of times and many times over; but without a stupefying drink, the lord does not..."}},{"n":62,"text":"गता द्विरष्टवर्षता ध्रुवोऽसि पञ्चविंशकः ।\nकुरुष्व धर्मसंचयं वयो हि तेऽतिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are twice eight years gone; you are twenty-five and steady; gather a store of dharma, for your age is passing."}},{"n":63,"text":"पुरा करोति सोऽन्तकः प्रमादगोमुखं दमम् ।\nयथागृहीतमुत्थितं त्वरस्व धर्मपालने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before that Ender makes his bridle of heedlessness, hurry to guard dharma as you took it up and have risen to it."}},{"n":64,"text":"यदा त्वमेव पृष्ठतस्त्वमग्रतो गमिष्यसि ।\nतथा गतिं गमिष्यतः किमात्मना परेण वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you yourself go behind and you go before, what use is self or other to one who is going that way?"}},{"n":65,"text":"यदेकपातिनां सतां भवत्यमुत्र गच्छताम् ।\nभयेषु सांपरायिकं निधत्स्व तं महानिधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What belongs to the good who go alone to the next world, in fears, lay up that great treasure for the beyond."}},{"n":66,"text":"सकूलमूलबान्धवं प्रभुर्हरत्यसङ्गवान् ।\nन सन्ति यस्य वारकाः कुरुष्व धर्मसंनिधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord, without attachment, carries off with root and kin; there are none who hold him back; make a treasury of dharma."}},{"n":67,"text":"इदं निदर्शनं मया तवेह पुत्र संमतम् ।\nस्वदर्शनानुमानतः प्रवर्णितं कुरुष्व तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This illustration I give you here, my son, accepted by me and described from my own insight and inference; do it."}},{"n":68,"text":"दधाति यः स्वकर्मणा धनानि यस्य कस्यचित् ।\nअबुद्धिमोहजैर्गुणैः शतैक एव युज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who by his own action provides wealth for anyone at all is joined, one among hundreds, with qualities born of folly."}},{"n":69,"text":"श्रुतं समर्थमस्तु ते प्रकुर्वतः शुभाः क्रियाः ।\nतदेव तत्र दर्शनं कृतज्ञमर्थसंहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"May what you have learned be effective for you as you do good acts; that is the view there, grateful and meaningful."}},{"n":70,"text":"निबन्धनी रज्जुरेषा या ग्रामे वसतो रतिः ।\nछित्त्वैनां सुकृतो यान्ति नैनां छिन्दन्ति दुष्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This rope binding is the delight of one who lives in the village; the virtuous go, having cut it; the wicked do not cut it."}},{"n":71,"text":"किं ते धनेन किं बन्धुभिस्ते\nकिं ते पुत्रैः पुत्रक यो मरिष्यसि ।\nआत्मानमन्विच्छ गुहां प्रविष्टं\nपितामहास्ते क्व गताश्च सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use to you are wealth, kinsmen or sons, my boy, you who will die? Seek the Self that has entered the cave; where have all your grandfathers gone?"}},{"n":72,"text":"श्वःकार्यमद्य कुर्वीत पूर्वाह्णे चापराह्णिकम् ।\nको हि तद्वेद कस्याद्य मृत्युसेना निवेक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should do tomorrow's work today, and the afternoon's in the forenoon; for who knows whose army of death will settle on whom today?"}},{"n":73,"text":"अनुगम्य श्मशानान्तं निवर्तन्तीह बान्धवाः ।\nअग्नौ प्रक्षिप्य पुरुषं ज्ञातयः सुहृदस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kinsmen follow to the end of the cremation ground and turn back, relatives and friends having thrown the man into the fire."}},{"n":74,"text":"नास्तिकान्निरनुक्रोशान्नरान्पापमतौ स्थितान् ।\nवामतः कुरु विश्रब्धं परं प्रेप्सुरतन्द्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turn away the unbelievers, the merciless, the men set on sinful thoughts, confidently to the left, if you wish for the highest, tireless."}},{"n":75,"text":"एवमभ्याहते लोके कालेनोपनिपीडिते ।\nसुमहद्धैर्यमालम्ब्य धर्मं सर्वात्मना कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the world struck so and pressed by time, take up great courage and practice dharma with your whole self."}},{"n":76,"text":"अथेमं दर्शनोपायं सम्यग्यो वेत्ति मानवः ।\nसम्यक्स धर्मं कृत्वेह परत्र सुखमेधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man who rightly knows this means of insight, having rightly done dharma here, prospers happily hereafter."}},{"n":77,"text":"न देहभेदे मरणं विजानतां\nन च प्रणाशः स्वनुपालिते पथि ।\nधर्मं हि यो वर्धयते स पण्डितो\nय एव धर्माच्च्यवते स मुह्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who know, there is no death in the breaking of the body, nor loss on a path well followed; one who increases dharma is wise, one who falls from dharma is deluded."}},{"n":78,"text":"प्रयुक्तयोः कर्मपथि स्वकर्मणोः\nफलं प्रयोक्ता लभते यथाविधि ।\nनिहीनकर्मा निरयं प्रपद्यते\nत्रिविष्टपं गच्छति धर्मपारगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of two deeds set on the path of action, the doer gets the fruit by rule; the one with poor deeds goes to hell, the one who has crossed dharma to heaven."}},{"n":79,"text":"सोपानभूतं स्वर्गस्य मानुष्यं प्राप्य दुर्लभम् ।\nतथात्मानं समादध्याद्भ्रश्येत न पुनर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having obtained the rare human birth, a ladder to heaven, set yourself so that you do not fall again."}},{"n":80,"text":"यस्य नोत्क्रामति मतिः स्वर्गमार्गानुसारिणी ।\nतमाहुः पुण्यकर्माणमशोच्यं मित्रबान्धवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Him whose mind, following the path to heaven, does not stray, they call a doer of merit, not to be grieved for by friends and kin."}},{"n":81,"text":"यस्य नोपहता बुद्धिर्निश्चयेष्ववलम्बते ।\nस्वर्गे कृतावकाशस्य तस्य नास्ति महद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One whose unharmed understanding holds firm in its resolves, having made room in heaven, has no great fear."}},{"n":82,"text":"तपोवनेषु ये जातास्तत्रैव निधनं गताः ।\nतेषामल्पतरो धर्मः कामभोगमजानताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those born in penance groves who died there, knowing nothing of enjoying desires, have smaller dharma."}},{"n":83,"text":"यस्तु भोगान्परित्यज्य शरीरेण तपश्चरेत् ।\nन तेन किंचिन्न प्राप्तं तन्मे बहुमतं फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But one who gives up enjoyments and practices austerity with the body has nothing unattained, and that fruit I hold in high regard."}},{"n":84,"text":"मातापितृसहस्राणि पुत्रदारशतानि च ।\nअनागतान्यतीतानि कस्य ते कस्य वा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of mothers and fathers, hundreds of sons and wives, future and past: whose are you, or whose are we?"}},{"n":85,"text":"न तेषां भवता कार्यं न कार्यं तव तैरपि ।\nस्वकृतैस्तानि यातानि भवांश्चैव गमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have no business with them, nor have they with you; they went by their own deeds, and so will you."}},{"n":86,"text":"इह लोके हि धनिनः परोऽपि स्वजनायते ।\nस्वजनस्तु दरिद्राणां जीवतामेव नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this world even a stranger becomes kin to the rich; but for the poor, kin vanish even while they live."}},{"n":87,"text":"संचिनोत्यशुभं कर्म कलत्रापेक्षया नरः ।\nततः क्लेशमवाप्नोति परत्रेह तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man gathers evil action out of regard for his wife; therefore he meets suffering both here and hereafter."}},{"n":88,"text":"पश्य त्वं छिद्रभूतं हि जीवलोकं स्वकर्मणा ।\nतत्कुरुष्व तथा पुत्र कृत्स्नं यत्समुदाहृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See that the world of the living is full of holes through its own actions; do so, my son, all that has been told."}},{"n":89,"text":"तदेतत्संप्रदृश्यैव कर्मभूमिं प्रविश्य ताम् ।\nशुभान्याचरितव्यानि परलोकमभीप्सता ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, having clearly seen this and having entered that field of action, one who desires the next world should do good deeds."}},{"n":90,"text":"मासर्तुसंज्ञापरिवर्तकेन\nसूर्याग्निना रात्रिदिवेन्धनेन ।\nस्वकर्मनिष्ठाफलसाक्षिकेण\nभूतानि कालः पचति प्रसह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the sun-fire that turns months, seasons and names, with night and day as fuel, and with deeds and devotion and their fruit as witnesses, Time cooks beings by force."}},{"n":91,"text":"धनेन किं यन्न ददाति नाश्नुते\nबलेन किं येन रिपून्न बाधते ।\nश्रुतेन किं येन न धर्ममाचरे-\nत्किमात्मना यो न जितेन्द्रियो वशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is wealth that is not given or enjoyed, strength that does not hold back foes, learning that does not lead to dharma, or a self that has not conquered its senses?"}},{"n":92,"text":"इदं द्वैपायनवचो हितमुक्तं निशम्य तु ।\nशुको गतः परित्यज्य पितरं मोक्षदेशिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard this beneficial speech of Dvaipayana, Shuka left his father, the teacher of liberation, and went away."}}]}]}